    "engine": "knitr",
    "markdown": "---\ntitle: \"Violin and half (split) violin plots in R with canvasXpress\"\ndescription: \"Show a full distribution per group as a violin, then split it in half to compare two conditions side by side — interactive and reproducible, in R.\"\nauthor: \"Isaac Neuhaus\"\ndate: \"2026-09-25\"\ncategories: [R, canvasXpress, violin, visualization]\nimage: \"thumbnail.png\"\n---\n\n\n\nA violin plot shows the **full shape of a distribution** — where the density is thick or thin —\ninstead of collapsing it to a box's quartiles. And when you want to compare two conditions at the\nsame position, a **split (half) violin** puts one condition on each half. Here we build both in R\nwith [canvasXpress](https://canvasxpress.org): interactive, and reproducible because the figure is\none portable spec.\n\n## The data\n\nA measurement across a few dose groups and two conditions. Swap in your own long-format table.\n\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nlibrary(canvasXpress)\n\nset.seed(1)\ndoses <- c(\"Low\", \"Medium\", \"High\"); conds <- c(\"Control\", \"Treated\")\nvalue <- c(); Dose <- c(); Condition <- c()\nfor (d in doses) for (co in conds) {\n  mu <- if (d == \"Low\") 6 else if (d == \"Medium\") 8 else 10\n  if (co == \"Treated\") mu <- mu + 1.5\n  value <- c(value, round(rnorm(40, mu, 1.2), 2))\n  Dose <- c(Dose, rep(d, 40)); Condition <- c(Condition, rep(co, 40))\n}\n```\n:::\n\n\n\nIn canvasXpress terms a violin is a `Boxplot` graph with the violin turned on: one measured variable\n× N observations, with the grouping columns as `smpAnnot`.\n\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nids <- paste0(\"o\", seq_along(value))\ny <- data.frame(matrix(value, nrow = 1, dimnames = list(\"value\", ids)), check.names = FALSE)\nsmpAnnot <- data.frame(Dose = Dose, Condition = Condition, row.names = ids, check.names = FALSE)\n```\n:::\n\n\n\n## A full violin per group\n\n`showViolinBoxplot = TRUE` draws the violin (with a small boxplot inside); `violinScale = \"area\"`\nmakes equal-area violins.\n\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\ncanvasXpress(\n  data = y, smpAnnot = smpAnnot, graphType = \"Boxplot\",\n  showViolinBoxplot = TRUE, violinScale = \"area\",\n  groupingFactors = list(\"Dose\"), xAxis = list(\"value\"),\n  smpTitle = \"Dose\", title = \"Distribution of value by dose\",\n  width = 650, height = 500\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<div id=\"htmlwidget-a3c87662a2939578a855\" style=\"width:100%;height:500px;\" class=\"canvasXpress html-widget\"></div>\n<script type=\"application/json\" data-for=\"htmlwidget-a3c87662a2939578a855\">{\"x\":{\"data\":{\"y\":{\"vars\":[\"value\"],\"smps\":[\"o1\",\"o2\",\"o3\",\"o4\",\"o5\",\"o6\",\"o7\",\"o8\",\"o9\",\"o10\",\"o11\",\"o12\",\"o13\",\"o14\",\"o15\",\"o16\",\"o17\",\"o18\",\"o19\",\"o20\",\"o21\",\"o22\",\"o23\",\"o24\",\"o25\",\"o26\",\"o27\",\"o28\",\"o29\",\"o30\",\"o31\",\"o32\",\"o33\",\"o34\",\"o35\",\"o36\",\"o37\",\"o38\",\"o39\",\"o40\",\"o41\",\"o42\",\"o43\",\"o44\",\"o45\",\"o46\",\"o47\",\"o48\",\"o49\",\"o50\",\"o51\",\"o52\",\"o53\",\"o54\",\"o55\",\"o56\",\"o57\",\"o58\",\"o59\",\"o60\",\"o61\",\"o62\",\"o63\",\"o64\",\"o65\",\"o66\",\"o67\",\"o68\",\"o69\",\"o70\",\"o71\",\"o72\",\"o73\",\"o74\",\"o75\",\"o76\",\"o77\",\"o78\",\"o79\",\"o80\",\"o81\",\"o82\",\"o83\",\"o84\",\"o85\",\"o86\",\"o87\",\"o88\",\"o89\",\"o90\",\"o91\",\"o92\",\"o93\",\"o94\",\"o95\",\"o96\",\"o97\",\"o98\",\"o99\",\"o100\",\"o101\",\"o102\",\"o103\",\"o104\",\"o105\",\"o106\",\"o107\",\"o108\",\"o109\",\"o110\",\"o111\",\"o112\",\"o113\",\"o114\",\"o115\",\"o116\",\"o117\",\"o118\",\"o119\",\"o120\",\"o121\",\"o122\",\"o123\",\"o124\",\"o125\",\"o126\",\"o127\",\"o128\",\"o129\",\"o130\",\"o131\",\"o132\",\"o133\",\"o134\",\"o135\",\"o136\",\"o137\",\"o138\",\"o139\",\"o140\",\"o141\",\"o142\",\"o143\",\"o144\",\"o145\",\"o146\",\"o147\",\"o148\",\"o149\",\"o150\",\"o151\",\"o152\",\"o153\",\"o154\",\"o155\",\"o156\",\"o157\",\"o158\",\"o159\",\"o160\",\"o16